# The site is fully prerendered — every route has its own HTML file, so the SPA
# fallback that used to serve index.html for unknown paths is gone. Without it,
# Cloudflare Pages serves the real 404.html with a real 404 status instead of a
# soft 404 that crawlers would treat as a duplicate of the home page.

# --- Legacy URLs from the React site --------------------------------------
# These paths are indexed. Rules are enumerated rather than globbed on purpose:
# a splat like /projects/* would shadow the real case-study pages below it.

# The blog became /writing. Only `welcome` has a successor post; the rest are
# not carried over, so they go to the hub rather than to a guessed equivalent.
/blog                        /writing              301
/blog/welcome                /writing/bienvenue    301
/blog/cache                  /writing              301
/blog/proxies                /writing              301
/blog/docker                 /writing              301
/blog/operating-systems      /writing              301
/blog/openai                 /writing              301

# Case studies were renamed. Two map onto a clear successor — auditex is the
# document-extraction product, architecture-brief-agent is the studio agents
# work. The others have no equivalent and go to the hub.
/projects/auditex                  /projects/extraction   301
/projects/architecture-brief-agent /projects/agents       301
/projects/growonline               /projects              301
/projects/legal-knowledge-ai       /projects              301
/projects/voicy                    /projects              301
/projects/autoscribe               /projects              301
/projects/portfolio                /projects              301
